      "type": "about",
      "tabLabel": "About",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Tute subastado",
          "subtitle": "Card Game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tute subastado: auction Tute. Trump or contract determined by auction/bidding. 40-card Spanish."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tute originated in Italy as tutti and spread to Spain in the 19th century, becoming one of the most popular card games there. Tute subastado is the auction variant: trump is not determined by a turned card but by a round of bidding; the highest bidder becomes soloist and chooses trump, and must make at least the number of points bid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two or more players."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard Spanish 40-card pack (four suits: oros, espadas, copas, bastos). In Tute subastado the twos are set aside and 36 cards are used; 12 cards are dealt to each player."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Cards"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "As Tute; then auction"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
